{"_ts": 1788890853.1162992, "url": "https://littlesis.org/api/entities/73433/connections?category_id=1", "body": {"meta": {"copyright": "LittleSis CC BY-SA 4.0", "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/", "apiVersion": "2.0"}, "data": [{"type": "entities", "id": 113, "attributes": {"id": 113, "name": "Raytheon Company", "blurb": "Defense contractor; merged with UTC. Surviving company exists as a subsidiary of the renamed UTC, company, Raytheon Technologies", "summary": "Raytheon is a major American defense contractor that specializes in defense and homeland security technology. As the world\u2019s largest producer of guided missiles, Raytheon specializes in manufacturing defense systems and defense electronics. \n\nA member of the defense electronic industry, Raytheon is most active lobbying on defense, homeland security and federal budget appropriation issues.", "website": "httpss://www.raytheon.com", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2026-01-06T23:05:11Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "923220", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["Raytheon", "Raytheon Company"], "types": ["Organization", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "Raytheon", "name_nick": "RAYTHEON", "employees": null, "revenue": 23247000000, "fedspending_id": "262102", "lda_registrant_id": "32828"}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "RTN", "sec_cik": 1047122}}, "tags": ["corporate-mapping-project", "icecontractor", "defence", "south-bay-la-power-structure"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/113-Raytheon_Company"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 39, "attributes": {"id": 39, "name": "RTX", "blurb": "The world's second-largest aerospace-and-defense company", "summary": "Publicly-traded defense and aerospace contractor, the result of mergers by UTC and Raytheon and the spin-offs of Otis Worldwide and Carrier ", "website": "https://www.rtx.com", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-05-21T16:59:25Z", "start_date": "1934-00-00", "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "1665246", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["IRS EIN 06-0570975", "RTX", "Raytheon Technologies", "Raytheon Technologies Corporation", "United Technologies", "United Technologies Corporation"], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "United Technologies", "name_nick": "UNITED_TECH", "employees": null, "revenue": 56098000000, "fedspending_id": "327319", "lda_registrant_id": "39267"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "RTX", "sec_cik": 101829}}, "tags": ["corporate-mapping-project", "fossil-fuel-industry", "corpu", "corpu-possible-duplicates"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/39-RTX"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 73, "attributes": {"id": 73, "name": "Johnson Controls", "blurb": "Smart Building Systems", "summary": "Johnson Controls: Enhancing the Intelligence of Buildings\r\nYour buildings have a purpose. \r\n\r\nThey are places for people to live or work. Facilities for learning or healing. Venues for entertainment and shopping. Sites for the specialized storage of tangible goods or mission-critical data. Your buildings have a huge variety of functions; they are central to your mission. \r\n\r\nThis is where Johnson Controls comes in, helping drive the outcomes that matter most. Through a full range of systems and digital solutions, we make your buildings smarter. A smarter building is safer, more comfortable, more efficient, and, ultimately, more sustainable. Most important, smarter buildings let you focus more intensely on your unique mission. Better for your people. Better for your bottom line. Better for the planet.\r\nAt Johnson Controls, we\u2019ve been making buildings smarter since 1885, and our capabilities, depth of innovation experience, and global reach have been growing ever since. Today, we offer the world\u2019s largest portfolio of building products, technologies, software, and services; we put that portfolio to work to transform the environments where people live, work, learn and play.\r\n\r\nJohnson Controls: The power behind your mission.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThe Power Behind Your Mission\r\n\r\nAt Johnson Controls, we transform the environments where people live, work, learn and play. From optimizing building performance to improving safety and enhancing comfort, we drive the outcomes that matter most.\r\n\r\nDedicated to protecting the environment, we deliver our promise in industries such as healthcare, education, data centers, and manufacturing.\r\nVIEW FULL-SCREEN VIDEO\r\n", "website": null, "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2025-03-21T03:44:18Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null, "connected_relationship_ids": "1703047", "connected_category_id": 1, "aliases": ["IRS EIN 39-0380010", "Johnson Controls", "Johnson Controls, Inc."], "types": ["Organization", "Business", "Public Company"], "extensions": {"Org": {"name": "Johnson Controls", "name_nick": "JOHN_CONTROL", "employees": null, "revenue": null, "fedspending_id": null, "lda_registrant_id": "51150"}, "Business": {"annual_profit": null, "assets": null, "marketcap": null, "net_income": null, "aum": null}, "PublicCompany": {"ticker": "JCI", "sec_cik": 53669}}, "tags": ["corporate-mapping-project"]}, "links": {"self": "https://littlesis.org/entities/73-Johnson_Controls"}}, {"type": "entities", "id": 34861, "attributes": {"id": 34861, "name": "Tyco International Plc", "blurb": "The world's largest dedicated fire protection and security company", "summary": "Tyco International plc, an Irish public limited company, as the successor registrant to Tyco International Ltd., a corporation organized under the laws of Switzerland.", "website": "http://www.tyco.com/", "parent_id": null, "primary_ext": "Org", "updated_at": "2023-03-24T16:41:50Z", "start_date": null, "end_date": null